IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `yoa-diversion`

-- Young Offenders Act 1994 (WA), ss 3, 4, 14, 22-23, 25, 27, 29-33, 41, 55 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_young-offenders-act-1994.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Scenario facts used (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake/facts.json): Jake born 2006-08-30; takes a phone case and
-- earbuds ($89) from a shop with two friends on 2021-11-20, aged 15, and is referred to a juvenile justice team (k021, k022);
-- the team on 2022-02-14 (k023): an apology, restitution, community work; k036 on 2026-11-20 (aged 20); k082 on 2047-03-04
-- (aged 40). The scenario does not say whether an infringement notice could have been given for the stealing, whether a
-- victim attended the team, or who attended with him; the fixtures assume no infringement notice, his mother and the store
-- manager present and agreeing, and both infringement-notice answers are asserted. Plain stealing is assumed not to be a
-- Schedule 1 or 2 offence: the deposit's Schedule 2 lists Criminal Code s 378(2) only for stealing a motor vehicle aggravated
-- by reckless or dangerous driving.

§ `Fixtures`

