§ `ss 3, 4 -- age and young person`

#ASSERT `age in completed years` 2006 8 30 2021 11 20 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `age in completed years` 2006 8 30 2022 2 14 EQUALS 15
#ASSERT `age in completed years` 2006 8 30 2047 3 4 EQUALS 40
#ASSERT `age in completed years` 2006 8 30 2024 8 29 EQUALS 17

#ASSERT `the Act applies to him as a young person for that offence` 15
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to him as a young person for that offence` 18

#ASSERT NOT `he is an independent young person` 15 TRUE
#ASSERT `he is an independent young person` 17 TRUE

§ `ss 22, 23 -- cautions`

#ASSERT `police may caution him instead of charging` `Jake's shop matter, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `police may caution him instead of charging` `the same matter had he been 18`
#ASSERT NOT `police may caution him instead of charging` `a robbery by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `police may caution him instead of charging` `a Weapons Act offence by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT `police may caution him instead of charging` `the shop matter where he denies responsibility`

#ASSERT `a caution is to be preferred to a charge` `Jake's shop matter, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `a caution is to be preferred to a charge` `the shop matter after an earlier finding of guilt`

§ `ss 25, 27, 29 -- referral to a juvenile justice team`

#ASSERT `police may refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `Jake's shop matter, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT NOT `police may refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `the same matter had he been 18`
#ASSERT NOT `police may refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `a robbery by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT `police may refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `a Weapons Act offence by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `police may refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `the shop matter where he denies responsibility`
#ASSERT NOT `police may refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `the shop matter where the store will not agree to a team`

#ASSERT NOT `an infringement notice is to be preferred to a referral` `Jake's shop matter, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT `an infringement notice is to be preferred to a referral` `the shop matter with an infringement notice available`
#ASSERT NOT `an infringement notice is to be preferred to a referral` `the shop matter where an infringement notice would be inappropriate`

#ASSERT `the discretion is to be exercised in favour of referral` `Jake's shop matter, 20 November 2021`
#ASSERT `the discretion is to be exercised in favour of referral` `the shop matter after an earlier caution`
#ASSERT NOT `the discretion is to be exercised in favour of referral` `the shop matter after an earlier finding of guilt`
#ASSERT NOT `the discretion is to be exercised in favour of referral` `the shop matter where he denies responsibility`

§ `s 41 -- what police may do`

#ASSERT `the option is open to police` `take no action` `a robbery by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `the option is open to police` `give a caution` `a robbery by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT NOT `the option is open to police` `refer the matter to a juvenile justice team` `a robbery by a 15-year-old`
#ASSERT `the option is open to police` `charge him without taking him into custody` `a robbery by a 15-year-old`

§ `ss 30, 31, 32 -- the team`

#ASSERT `the team may proceed` `Jake's team hearing with his mother and the store manager`
#ASSERT NOT `the team may proceed` `a hearing with no responsible adult`
#ASSERT `the team may proceed` `a hearing where the victim objects to the terms`
#ASSERT `the team may proceed` `a hearing where a substitute adult stands in`

#ASSERT `the team may dispose of the matter` `Jake's team hearing with his mother and the store manager`
#ASSERT NOT `the team may dispose of the matter` `a hearing with no responsible adult`
#ASSERT NOT `the team may dispose of the matter` `a hearing where the victim objects to the terms`
#ASSERT `the team may dispose of the matter` `a hearing where a substitute adult stands in`

§ `s 33 -- completing the terms`

#ASSERT `what a court must do with a later charge` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the charge must be dismissed without being determined`
#ASSERT `what a court must do with a later charge` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the court deals with him, having regard to the steps he took`
#ASSERT `what a court must do with a later charge` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the court deals with him`

